@@ -1,5 +1,21 @@
 # deploy-demo
 
-Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main`.
+Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main` and on every pushed version
+tag matching `v*` (e.g. `v1.2.0`). It can also be started manually via
+`workflow_dispatch`.
+
+## AWS authentication
+
+The workflow authenticates with GitHub OIDC; there are no long-lived AWS access
+keys. It assumes `arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/deploy-widget` in `eu-north-1`
+and requires the `id-token: write` permission (already set in the workflow).
+
+The role's trust policy must allow `token.actions.githubusercontent.com` as a
+federated principal, with `aud` = `sts.amazonaws.com` and a `sub` condition
+limited to this repository's refs, e.g. `repo:<owner>/<repo>:ref:refs/heads/main`
+and `repo:<owner>/<repo>:ref:refs/tags/v*`.
+
+The old `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` repository secrets are no
+longer used and should be deleted. `SLACK_WEBHOOK` is still required.
 
 This repository is public.
